# DURABLE REPRO — D10 exclusivity hole #4: a for-loop body mutates the ITERABLE
# through a `&`-arg free call.
#
# The iterable guard (`check_expr.rs`'s for-loop arm) catches a DIRECT `v.push`
# in the body, but a mutation that happens behind a call boundary — `grow(&v)` —
# is opaque to it. The loop then walks a reallocated backing store.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg, C backend, `--sanitize`): `gg check`
# clean, then
#   AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free ... READ of size 32 ...
#   in gorget_string_borrow
# reported at the loop's element read.
#
# INTENDED: REJECTED at `gg check` with `E_BorrowConflict`, exactly as the
# direct `v.push(...)` spelling in the same position already is. The `&` sigil
# is not a way to launder a mutation past the iterable guard.
#
# ⚠ SHAPE PRECISION, recorded because the obvious minimal shape is a FALSE
# NEGATIVE: with a SINGLE-element collection the program runs clean (measured).
# The loop must survive PAST the reallocation to touch freed memory, so the
# collection needs ≥2 elements and the mutation must happen before the last
# iteration's element read. That is why this fixture seeds three elements and
# puts `grow(&v)` after the print.
#
# The 4096-push loop FORCES a real reallocation.
#
#
# ORACLE (ggdef, measured this session): ACCEPTS this program and prints the
# pre-mutation value. ggdef is a definitional INTERPRETER with value semantics,
# so a reallocation cannot invalidate anything and this UAF class is
# structurally unobservable in that lane — it is NOT the authority here. The
# intended REJECT comes from the ratified D10 exclusivity ruling, which ggdef
# owes as part of the same landing (Core #9). Full note in
# `sound_excl_getchain_local.gg`.
# Cited from TODO.md (CoW / ownership / High): the D10 "one exclusive writer"
# structural-chokepoint entry, hole #4.
void grow(Vector[String] &v):
    int i = 0
    while i < 4096:
        v.push("filler-padding-to-force-a-real-reallocation")
        i = i + 1

void main():
    Vector[String] v = Vector[String]()
    v.push("alpha-heap-forced-payload")
    v.push("beta-heap-forced-payload")
    v.push("gamma-heap-forced-payload")
    for x in v:
        print(x)
        grow(&v)
